WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.499
Landing requires someone on
site who operates the system.

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:10.011
Name the owner and clarify routine responsibilities,
escalation, exceptions, and the authority

00:00:10.081 --> 00:00:11.681
to disable the workflow.

00:00:11.751 --> 00:00:14.930
Ownership is more than listing
a person in a document.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.755
The person needs context,
access, capability, and time.

00:00:18.825 --> 00:00:24.158
Keep your accountability through adoption while
transferring practical capability rather than

00:00:24.228 --> 00:00:26.148
preserving dependence on you.

00:00:26.218 --> 00:00:29.909
Maya owns the queue, but Luis
alone can restore the service.

00:00:29.979 --> 00:00:35.483
If Luis is unavailable, agents need a
manual fallback and an escalation contact.

00:00:35.553 --> 00:00:40.118
A nominal owner without a recovery
path cannot operate independently.

00:00:40.188 --> 00:00:44.967
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

00:00:45.037 --> 00:00:49.218
Write an ownership table and a one-page
runbook with a manual fallback.

00:00:49.288 --> 00:00:54.835
The runbook describes availability checks,
failed-request symptoms, the routing-rule version,

00:00:54.905 --> 00:01:00.579
manual category lookup, escalation to Luis,
and the conditions for disabling assistance.

00:01:00.649 --> 00:01:05.108
Maya can make the disable decision
within the agreed workflow authority.

00:01:05.178 --> 00:01:07.525
Priya controls data-access changes.

00:01:07.595 --> 00:01:13.931
A support rotation covers absence rather than
making the original engineer the only responder.

00:01:14.001 --> 00:01:16.070
What makes ownership operational?

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.868
A. A name on a slide B.

00:01:17.938 --> 00:01:21.842
Authority, capability, access,
and recovery instructions C.

00:01:21.912 --> 00:01:24.067
The engineer always being online.

00:01:24.137 --> 00:01:25.609
The best answer is B.

00:01:25.679 --> 00:01:28.879
Ownership must survive
ordinary absence and failure.
